# Keep Rust source files as LF in the repository, regardless of a contributor's
# core.autocrlf setting. This prevents Windows checkouts from committing CRLF and
# producing whole-file diffs / merge conflicts in the source the team edits.
#
# Deliberately scoped to *.rs: the rest of the repo (docs, workflows, etc.) was
# historically committed with CRLF, and forcing eol=lf on it would trigger a
# mass renormalization unrelated to any current change.
*.rs    text eol=lf

# .ngit/act/workflows/ is generated from .github/workflows/ by .ngit/act/sync.sh
# and is never hand-edited. Marking it generated collapses it in GitHub's
# Files-changed view, so a reviewer sees the lines that need judgement rather
# than a few thousand mirrored ones.
#
# A new line on a new path pattern: it does not widen the *.rs eol=lf scope
# above, so it triggers none of the renormalization that comment warns about.
.ngit/act/workflows/**   linguist-generated=true
